# ============================================================================
# SharkPay CODEOWNERS — mirrors the isolation rules of ADR 003 §2
# (docs/adr/003-safe-parallelism-and-verification.md).
#
# ADR 003 §2.1: "One agent = one module = one directory." Shared root files
# are owned by the integrator EXCLUSIVELY. CODEOWNERS makes the integrator
# the required reviewer on every path and calls out the integrator-only
# seams explicitly so neither humans nor automation mistake them for
# workstream territory.
#
# There is exactly one committer/reviewer: @Roy-Wanyoike, the integrator
# role of ADR 003 §2.3 (all branch/commit/push/PR operations are
# centralised there — no agent touches git). "Stricter ownership" below is
# therefore expressed as dedicated rules + commentary marking these paths
# as integration-time decisions, not as a second reviewer.
#
# NOTE (CODEOWNERS precedence): the LAST matching rule wins, so the
# specific rules below intentionally come after the `*` default.
# ============================================================================

# ── Default: the integrator reviews everything ─────────────────────────────
* @Roy-Wanyoike

# ── Integrator-only shared seams (ADR 003 §2.1, §2.2, §1) ──────────────────

# CI + repo governance: what "verified" means may only change in an
# integrator commit that re-runs the full G1–G5 ladder. The canonical gate
# is .github/workflows/verify.yml (mirror of scripts/verify-all.sh);
# workflows/ci.yml is retired by the integrator.
/.github/           @Roy-Wanyoike
/.github/workflows/ @Roy-Wanyoike

# Contracts are the ONLY integration seam between the Go and Java runtimes
# (ADR 002/003 §2.2) and are APPEND-ONLY: merged contract files are frozen,
# new uniquely-named files are allowed, and any other change is an
# integration-time decision. Parallel workstreams must never modify these.
/contracts/ @Roy-Wanyoike

# Shared platform pre-stage (ADR 003 §1): the cross-runtime money libraries
# (packages/go/money, packages/java/sharkpay-money) are the 1:1 semantic
# anchor for every balance in the system; toolchain pins live here too.
# Integrator-only — a workstream touching these defeats the whole protocol.
/packages/ @Roy-Wanyoike

# Remaining shared root files explicitly named integrator-only by ADR 003
# §2.1 (docker-compose.yml, Makefile, go.work, root poms, scripts):
/docker-compose.yml @Roy-Wanyoike
/Makefile           @Roy-Wanyoike
/go.work            @Roy-Wanyoike
/scripts/           @Roy-Wanyoike
